.TH V23-PRINCIPAL 1
.SH NAME
v23/principal \- create a Vanadium principal and print a self-blessing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v23/principal
[
.B -b
.I bits
]
[
.B -n
.I name
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I V23/principal
creates an in-memory Vanadium principal
.RI ( v23-security (2)),
self-blesses it as
.I name
(default
.BR principal ),
trusts that blessing as a root, and prints the public key, blessing name(s),
and
.IR v23 (6)
encoding of the blessings.
.PP
.B -b
sets Elgamal key size in bits (default 512).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/v23/principal.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v23-intro (2),
.IR v23-security (2),
.IR v23 (6),
.IR v23-selftest (1)
.SH BUGS
.IP \(bu
Does not write keys or blessings to disk; output is for inspection/demo only.
.IP \(bu
Large
.B -b
values make key generation very slow.
